- The answer--

00:01:43.344 --> 00:01:44.799
Who asked the question, again?

00:01:44.799 --> 00:01:45.750
- [India] Neil.

00:01:45.750 --> 00:01:49.221
- Neil, it sounds like, by
the way you're asking the

00:01:49.221 --> 00:01:51.454
question, I'm glad we're
getting to attack this,

00:01:51.454 --> 00:01:53.953
that you're looking at what is deemed as

00:01:53.953 --> 00:01:56.406
"Internet Marketing", right?
When you say that all marketing

00:01:56.406 --> 00:01:58.854
jobs are scummy out of school,
I think what you're falling

00:01:58.854 --> 00:02:02.869
into, is kind of those
e-book, kind of landing page,

00:02:02.869 --> 00:02:06.880
the bad version of all these
great growth hackers out there,

00:02:06.880 --> 00:02:09.439
the bad version of that, right?
Lowest common denominator,

00:02:09.439 --> 00:02:12.737
playing arbitrage, internet
marketing, buy my e-book

00:02:12.737 --> 00:02:15.783
in the back room, and the discs, MLM.

00:02:15.783 --> 00:02:18.044
It sounds like you're going down a funnel,

00:02:18.044 --> 00:02:21.408
and what you deem as marketing
is scummy, and I understand

00:02:21.408 --> 00:02:25.594
a lot of that gets into dark
marketing but 98% of the

00:02:25.594 --> 00:02:28.644
marketing jobs in the world are
like working at VaynerMedia,

00:02:28.644 --> 00:02:31.994
this is marketing. So
first of all, I recommend

00:02:31.994 --> 00:02:34.616
recalibrating how you're
positioning marketing,

00:02:34.616 --> 00:02:36.472
and make sure that you're not
going down the rabbit hole

00:02:36.472 --> 00:02:38.926
of "Internet Marketing", and
I keep quoting it like this--

00:02:38.926 --> 00:02:41.367
First, I love air quotes and
we all know that but second,

00:02:41.367 --> 00:02:45.138
there is that term for just
copywriting, make landing pages

00:02:45.138 --> 00:02:48.281
of red and yellow, and buy
this, and whether you're selling

00:02:48.281 --> 00:02:50.510
supplements, or an e-book, or information,

00:02:50.510 --> 00:02:53.506
play that game out, that's
not the world of marketing

00:02:53.506 --> 00:02:56.023
that I believe in or think about.

00:02:56.023 --> 00:03:00.271
So I would tell you that there
are eight billion agencies

00:03:00.271 --> 00:03:03.596
marketing, digital,
social agencies out there,

00:03:03.596 --> 00:03:06.030
and I would immediately
go get an internship,

00:03:06.030 --> 00:03:08.753
if you can't get a job, and
prove that you've got the chops.

00:03:08.753 --> 00:03:12.268
It's unbelievable how high of
a percentage of the interns

00:03:12.268 --> 00:03:13.662
that we get here at VaynerMedia

00:03:13.662 --> 00:03:15.839
we offer a job to. One, we're growing fast,

00:03:15.839 --> 00:03:18.150
so that makes sense, but they've
come in and they've hustled

00:03:18.150 --> 00:03:22.693
and so the lack of
internship, out of college,

00:03:22.693 --> 00:03:25.744
if the market is bad, blows me away.

00:03:25.744 --> 00:03:27.576
It seems like the market
is getting better,

00:03:27.576 --> 00:03:29.595
jobs are being created more at this scale,

00:03:29.595 --> 00:03:32.701
than say, 24-36 months ago.
But the famous DRock story,

00:03:32.701 --> 00:03:34.856
or any other story like,
the ability for you to go

00:03:34.856 --> 00:03:38.048
and work for somebody pro
bono to get a résumé--

00:03:38.048 --> 00:03:41.774
Look, to me, if you're
struggling to get a job for

00:03:41.774 --> 00:03:44.128
two, three, four, five
months out of school,

00:03:44.128 --> 00:03:47.238
why in the world you wouldn't
take a half of your day,

00:03:47.238 --> 00:03:50.917
each day, to then work
somewhere for free, or intern,

00:03:50.917 --> 00:03:55.696
whatever it is, to a) pick
up skills, b) network,

00:03:55.696 --> 00:03:58.471
c) learn your craft in
action and watch it,

00:03:58.471 --> 00:04:01.288
d) create the leverage and
almost guilt your employer

00:04:01.288 --> 00:04:03.835
into hiring you, or making
them tell somebody else

00:04:03.835 --> 00:04:06.860
to hire you. You know,
better than sitting around

00:04:06.860 --> 00:04:08.795
and moping about why it's not working out.

00:04:08.795 --> 00:04:12.331
Unless you're out there,
literally, in job interviews

00:04:12.331 --> 00:04:16.392
or sending résumés, you've
got 18 hours in a day

00:04:16.392 --> 00:04:19.809
to execute this. To me, you
could be doing that from

00:04:19.809 --> 00:04:22.451
seven p.m. to two in the morning, and then

00:04:22.451 --> 00:04:24.657
from nine to seven, you could go do it.

00:04:24.657 --> 00:04:27.533
Go work at a pro bono place, or a museum,

00:04:27.533 --> 00:04:30.817
put your skills into action
if you're a marketer.

